# Round 71: aot_call_name/_ic lacked the non-callable guard their sibling
# aot_call_value already had (the round-70 sibling-asymmetry pattern) --
# call_eigs_fn returns null with NO error flag for a non-FN, so calling a
# string through an alias printed null, rc 0, where the VM raises "cannot
# call str" rc 1. The unboxed-numeric variant died with a FALSE reason
# ("undefined function 'x'" for a defined variable); the emitter now
# emits the VM's own "cannot call num" for statically-known numeric
# callees, at the call's reachability. _err class: both die, equal codes.
x is "hello"
g is x
print of "before"
z is g of 1
print of z
